Why the lines move: the fix mints one public error code, `CYCLIC_ARTIFACT_PACKAGES` (named by the seat on the siblings' "adjective + ARTIFACT_PACKAGE(S)" pattern), registered in `ERROR_CODE_LEDGER` beside `INVALID_ARTIFACT_PACKAGES`, `INVALID_ARTIFACT_PACKAGE_ENTRY` and `DUPLICATE_ARTIFACT_PACKAGE`: `422`, `details.cycle` listing the package ids along the cycle. A cycle answered `500 INTERNAL_ERROR` before (measured through a real HonoHttpServer) and is refused with a typed 422 after; nothing accepted before is refused. The review owed becomes contract tier (a `packages/spec/src` path), and landing goes through the seat's governed step.

File surface (replaces the claim's): 
- `packages/core/src/artifact-packages.ts` (`resolveArtifactPackageEntries` refuses a cycle with the new code), `packages/core/src/plugin-order.ts` (a non-breaking `PluginOrderCycleError extends Error` carrying `cycle`, same message, so boot callers see no change), their tests;
- `packages/spec/src/api/error-code-ledger.zod.ts` (the new row) and whatever generated artifacts and ledgers the new `ErrorCode` member moves;
- `packages/cloud-connection/src/marketplace-install-local-plugin.ts`: step 1c (`unrunnableCode`) gains the `declaredRefusalAnswer` catch steps 2a/2b/2c″ already have, since over the real runtime it meets the resolver first and today lets every resolver refusal (the three siblings included) reach the transport as a 500; `declaredRefusalAnswer` forwards the refusal's `details`; its docblock; install-local tests over the real runtime (no mock) for the cycle and the siblings, and the cycle case of `marketplace-install-local-resolver-refusal-34432.test.ts`;
- `packages/plugins/plugin-dev/src/dev-i18n-packages-reader.test.ts` (its cycle pin) and `dev-i18n.ts` docblock; `packages/runtime/src/artifact-collections.ts` header comment;
- `.changeset/`.
The step-1c fix closes the family here; no separate card is filed for the siblings' 500.
